  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Two token classes, one gate",
      "items": [
        "Operator: router.localToken — every route, no ceiling.",
        "Apps: a router.apps row — its own token, grant ceiling, and workspace root.",
        "The /api control plane is operator-only: an app token gets 403 there and acts through /v1.",
        "POST /api/keys is write-only — the response says whether a name resolves, never the value (router/server.js:2202).",
        "A spawn past the ceiling is a 403 that names the ceiling (router/server.js:1849).",
        "The durable memory plane: /v1/memory is capability-gated by the app's ceiling; /api/memory is operator-only (router/server.js:2244)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What kit apply owns",
      "items": [
        "Copies router/ into the runtime dir; the service runs that copy, so git pull never moves it.",
        "Renders config.json from roster.json and writes env-var names into .env (chmod 600).",
        "The dashboard saves through the same CLI, not a second copy (router/server.js:1073); kit quickstart runs the same steps with prompts.",
        "The memory store is runtime state under the kit home — kit memory stats/search/gc/import and the MCP server read and write it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Degradation is the contract",
      "items": [
        "A judge outage, a missing key, or an exhausted quota walks the candidate chain instead of failing.",
        "Every attempt, successful or not, lands in the usage ledger."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The plane calls back through the router",
      "items": [
        "Plane defaults: baseUrl 127.0.0.1:8300, token local-auto-router (lib/workflow/engine.mjs:105).",
        "Judgments ride sys1.classify / sys1.judge, journalled per run (lib/workflow/engine.mjs:551)."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
